WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.997
A schema is also a contract for

00:00:02.024 --> 00:00:07.491
future users Consistent naming named constraints
ERDs

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.688
and a data dictionary make the structure

00:00:09.715 --> 00:00:14.471
easier to understand Change management matters
because

00:00:14.485 --> 00:00:18.935
schemas evolve Use versioned migrations review
important

00:00:18.948 --> 00:00:20.724
changes and test how to roll them

00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:25.656
back Security includes least privilege separation of

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:30.790
sensitive data and access auditing Reliability
includes

00:00:30.803 --> 00:00:34.659
backups restore testing quality monitoring ownership
and

00:00:34.685 --> 00:00:39.418
lineage For analytics document more than column

00:00:39.444 --> 00:00:43.499
names Record table grain source owner refresh

00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:45.446
behavior and how the data moves from

00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:50.198
source systems into analytical outputs Good
governance

00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:52.316
helps people trust not only the database

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:54.540
structure but also the meaning and history

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:55.237
of the data
